StrategyManager::initialize(address _registry, FeeConfig _feeConfig)
├── Given _registry is zero address
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientZeroRegistry
├── Given performanceFeeBps exceeds MAX_PERFORMANCE_FEE_BPS
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerInvalidPerformanceFeeBps
├── Given daoTreasury is zero address
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerZeroDaoTreasury
├── Given valid parameters
│   ├── It should store registry reference in ERC-7201 namespaced storage (RegistryClientUpgradeable)
│   ├── It should store daoTreasury and performanceFeeBps from FeeConfig
│   ├── It should initialize UUPS upgradeable
│   ├── It should initialize RegistryClient
│   ├── It should initialize pausable
│   ├── It should initialize reentrancy guard
│   ├── It should emit Initialized event (with registry address)
│   ├── It should emit DaoTreasuryChanged (initial is zero address)
│   ├── It should emit PerformanceFeeBpsChanged (initial is zero)
│   └── It should NOT grant roles locally (ADMIN/CONTROLLER live on Registry)
└── Given already initialized
    └── It should revert with InvalidInitialization

StrategyManager::addStrategy(address _strategy, uint8 _depositWeight, uint8 _withdrawalWeight)
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── Given strategy address is zero
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerZeroAddress
├── Given strategy has no contract code
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerNoCode
├── Given strategy is already registered
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerStrategyAlreadyRegistered
├── Given depositWeight exceeds MAX_DEPOSIT_WEIGHT
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerInvalidDepositWeight
├── Given withdrawalWeight exceeds MAX_WITHDRAWAL_WEIGHT
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerInvalidWithdrawalWeight
├── Given zero depositWeight and/or withdrawalWeight
│   ├── It should add the strategy successfully (zero is allowed)
│   └── It should store the zero weight(s)
├── Given contract is paused
│   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── Given valid parameters
│   ├── It should add strategy to EnumerableSet (via add)
│   ├── It should store depositWeight and withdrawalWeight
│   ├── It should emit StrategyAdded event (with strategy address)
│   ├── It should emit DepositWeightUpdated and WithdrawalWeightUpdated
│   └── It should NOT set initial NAV (strategies report their own NAV via navInETH())
├── Given removeStrategy then re-add with performance fees enabled
│   ├── It should not mint phantom fees immediately after registration
│   ├── It should block phantom fee minting on repeated remove-re-add harvest loops
│   └── It should still fee real LP gains after re-registration
└── Given reentrancy attack
    └── It should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall

StrategyManager::setDepositWeight(address _strategy, uint8 _depositWeight)
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── Given strategy is not registered
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerStrategyNotRegistered
├── Given depositWeight exceeds MAX_DEPOSIT_WEIGHT
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerInvalidDepositWeight
└── Given valid parameters
    ├── It should update depositWeight
    └── It should emit DepositWeightUpdated

StrategyManager::setWithdrawalWeight(address _strategy, uint8 _withdrawalWeight)
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── Given strategy is not registered
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerStrategyNotRegistered
├── Given withdrawalWeight exceeds MAX_WITHDRAWAL_WEIGHT
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerInvalidWithdrawalWeight
└── Given valid parameters
    ├── It should update withdrawalWeight
    └── It should emit WithdrawalWeightUpdated

StrategyManager::setStrategyWeights(address[] _strategies, uint8[] _depositWeights, uint8[] _withdrawalWeights)
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── Given array lengths mismatch
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerInvalidLength
├── Given a strategy in the list is not registered
│   ├── It should revert with StrategyManagerStrategyNotRegistered
│   └── It should leave earlier strategies' weights unchanged (no partial update)
├── Given a weight in the list exceeds MAX_DEPOSIT_WEIGHT or MAX_WITHDRAWAL_WEIGHT
│   ├── It should revert with StrategyManagerInvalidDepositWeight / StrategyManagerInvalidWithdrawalWeight
│   └── It should leave earlier strategies' weights unchanged (no partial update)
└── Given valid parameters
    ├── It should atomically update depositWeight and withdrawalWeight for each strategy
    └── It should emit DepositWeightUpdated and WithdrawalWeightUpdated per strategy

StrategyManager::removeStrategy(address _strategy)
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── Given strategy is not registered
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerStrategyNotRegistered
├── Given strategy NAV in ETH exceeds MAX_NAV_RESIDUE
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerStrategyNAVResidueTooHigh
├── Given strategy navInETH reverts
│   └── It should revert (bubbles the strategy revert; use forceRemoveStrategy)
├── Given strategy NAV in ETH is at most MAX_NAV_RESIDUE
│   ├── It should remove the strategy successfully
│   ├── It should clear depositWeight and withdrawalWeight to 0
│   └── It should emit StrategyRemoved
├── Given contract is paused
│   ├── It should remove the strategy successfully (escape hatch; unlike addStrategy)
│   └── It should emit StrategyRemoved
├── Given valid parameters
│   ├── It should remove strategy from EnumerableSet (via remove)
│   ├── It should clear depositWeight and withdrawalWeight to 0
│   ├── It should preserve lastStrategyWithdrawal (cooldown survives remove → re-add)
│   ├── It should best-effort revoke CONVERTER_CALLER_ROLE via the Converter
│   ├── It should emit StrategyRemoved
│   └── It should NOT subtract NAV (NAV is read from strategy, not stored)
└── Given reentrancy attack
    └── It should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall

StrategyManager::forceRemoveStrategy(address _strategy)
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── Given strategy is not registered
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerStrategyNotRegistered
├── Given strategy NAV in ETH exceeds MAX_NAV_RESIDUE (over-reporting strategy)
│   ├── It should NOT revert (unlike removeStrategy)
│   ├── It should remove the strategy successfully
│   ├── It should clear depositWeight and withdrawalWeight to 0
│   ├── It should emit StrategyForceRemoved with the reported NAV and navReverted false
│   └── It should unfreeze totalNAVInETH (over-reported NAV no longer summed)
├── Given strategy navInETH reverts
│   ├── It should remove the strategy successfully
│   ├── It should clear depositWeight and withdrawalWeight to 0
│   └── It should emit StrategyForceRemoved with reportedNAV zero and navReverted true
├── Given contract is paused
│   ├── It should remove the strategy successfully (escape hatch; unlike addStrategy)
│   └── It should emit StrategyForceRemoved
├── Given valid parameters
│   ├── It should remove strategy from EnumerableSet (via remove)
│   ├── It should clear depositWeight and withdrawalWeight to 0
│   ├── It should best-effort revoke CONVERTER_CALLER_ROLE (like removeStrategy)
│   ├── It should preserve lastStrategyWithdrawal (shared _deregisterStrategy)
│   └── It should NOT require the strategy to be paused (broken strategies may misreport paused())
└── Given reentrancy attack
    └── It should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall

StrategyManager::orphaned strategy recovery (IStrategy.emergencyExit)
├── Given strategy was force-removed while navInETH reverted and strategy still holds ETH
│   ├── It should exclude orphaned ETH from totalNAVInETH
│   ├── It should send orphaned ETH to StrategyManager on emergencyExit()
│   ├── It should emit EmergencyExited on the strategy
│   └── It should include recovered ETH in totalNAVInETH
├── Given strategy is still registered and calls emergencyExit
│   └── It should write off pending LP fees (charged = earned; pending fees zero after emergencyExit)

StrategyManager::depositToStrategies(uint256 _amount)
├── Given caller is not the registered Controller
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientInvalidCaller
├── Given contract is paused
│   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── Given no strategies are registered
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerNoStrategiesRegistered
├── Given all strategies are unhealthy (maxDeposit > 0)
│   ├── It should return zero
│   ├── It should NOT deposit to any strategy
│   └── It should return all ETH to controller
├── Given all strategies are unhealthy or have zero maxDeposit
│   ├── It should return zero
│   ├── It should NOT deposit to any strategy
│   └── It should return all ETH to controller
├── Given all strategies are cooling down after a withdrawal (strategyDepositCooldown > 0)
│   ├── It should return zero
│   ├── It should NOT deposit to any strategy
│   └── It should return all ETH to controller
├── Given valid parameters
│   ├── It should calculate deposit amounts based on depositWeight (proportional weighting)
│   ├── It should skip strategies with zero depositWeight (no share of allocation; no revert)
│   ├── It should respect maxDeposit limits for each strategy
│   ├── It should skip unhealthy strategies
│   ├── It should skip strategies cooling down after a withdrawal (strategyDepositCooldown > 0)
│   ├── It should deposit funds to healthy strategies (via strategy.deposit())
│   ├── It should emit FundsDepositedToStrategy event for each strategy
│   ├── It should emit StrategyDepositFailed(strategy, reason) and continue when one strategy.deposit() reverts
│   ├── It should return remaining funds to controller if any
│   └── It should handle proportional deposit correctly
└── Given reentrancy attack
    └── It should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall

StrategyManager::depositToStrategies(uint256 _startIndex, uint256 _endIndex, uint256 _amount)
├── Given caller is not the registered Controller
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientInvalidCaller
├── Given contract is paused
│   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── Given no strategies are registered
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerNoStrategiesRegistered
├── Given invalid range (endIndex > strategies.length or startIndex >= endIndex)
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerInvalidRange
├── Given no strategies in range are healthy or have zero maxDeposit
│   ├── It should return zero
│   ├── It should NOT deposit to any strategy in range
│   └── It should return all ETH to controller
├── Given valid parameters
│   ├── It should calculate deposit amounts based on depositWeight only for strategies in range
│   ├── It should skip strategies in range with zero depositWeight (no share of allocation; no revert)
│   ├── It should respect maxDeposit limits for each strategy in range
│   ├── It should skip unhealthy strategies in range
│   ├── It should skip strategies in range cooling down after a withdrawal (strategyDepositCooldown > 0)
│   ├── It should deposit funds only to healthy strategies in the specified range
│   ├── It should emit FundsDepositedToStrategy event for each strategy in range
│   ├── It should emit StrategyDepositFailed(strategy, reason) and continue when one strategy.deposit() reverts
│   ├── It should return remaining funds to controller if any
│   └── It should handle proportional deposit correctly within the range
└── Given reentrancy attack
    └── It should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall

StrategyManager::depositToStrategy(address _strategy, uint256 _amount)
├── Given caller is not the registered Controller
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientInvalidCaller
├── Given strategy is not registered
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerStrategyNotRegistered
├── Given contract is paused
│   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── Given strategy has zero maxDeposit
│   ├── It should return zero
│   └── It should return all ETH to controller
├── Given strategy is cooling down after a withdrawal (strategyDepositCooldown > 0)
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerStrategyInDepositCooldown
├── Given strategyDepositCooldown > 0 but strategy has never been withdrawn from
│   └── It should deposit normally (lastStrategyWithdrawal == 0 never triggers the cooldown)
├── Given strategyDepositCooldown is zero (default)
│   └── It should deposit normally even immediately after a withdrawal
├── Given valid parameters
│   ├── It should deposit funds to strategy (via strategy.deposit())
│   ├── It should respect maxDeposit limit
│   ├── It should emit FundsDepositedToStrategy event
│   └── It should return remaining funds to controller if amount exceeds maxDeposit
├── Given strategy.deposit() reverts
│   └── It should revert (strict single-strategy path)
└── Given reentrancy attack
    └── It should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall

StrategyManager::withdrawFromStrategies(uint256 _amount)
├── Given caller is not the registered Controller
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientInvalidCaller
├── Given contract is paused
│   └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── Given no strategies are registered
│   └── It should revert with StrategyManagerNoStrategiesRegistered
├── Given no strategies have available liquidity (maxWithdrawal == 0)
│   ├── It should return zero
│   └── It should NOT call strategy.withdraw on any strategy
├── Given valid parameters
│   ├── It should harvest accrued performance fees in one EVE mint before any withdrawal
│   ├── It should emit StrategyHarvestFailed(strategy, reason) and continue when one settlePerformanceFee() reverts during pre-withdraw harvest
│   ├── It should calculate withdrawal based on withdrawalWeight (proportional weighting)
│   ├── It should skip strategies with zero withdrawalWeight (no share of allocation; no revert)
│   ├── It should respect maxWithdrawal limits for each strategy
│   ├── It should withdraw funds from strategies (via strategy.withdraw(controller, amount))
│   ├── It should record lastStrategyWithdrawal for each strategy withdrawn from (starts the deposit cooldown)
│   ├── It should NOT be blocked by an active cooldown (withdrawals are exempt so exit liquidity is never blocked)
│   ├── It should emit FundsWithdrawnFromStrategy with net ETH received by controller (balance delta across withdraw())
│   ├── It should emit StrategyWithdrawFailed(strategy, reason) and continue when one strategy.withdraw() reverts
│   └── It should handle proportional withdrawal correctly
└── Given reentrancy attack
    └── It should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall

